      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `UtcInstant.equals()` returns `false` when compared to a non-`UtcInstant` object (a `StringBuffer`), and also checks the MJD and nanoOfDay values for epoch+3s. I'll improve variable names, add a meaningful test method name, and clarify intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test adds descriptive constants (`MJD_OF_UNIX_EPOCH`, `NANOS_PER_SECOND`), renames variables to clarify their roles, gives the test method a meaningful name, and adds assertion messages that explain the intent — all without changing the methods called or their arguments."
